WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.261
(bright music)

00:00:01.261 --> 00:00:03.670
- [Narrator] After years of development,

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.110
legacy Detroit automakers,

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:06.520
General Motors and Ford,

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.317
are now entering the
market for electric trucks.

00:00:09.317 --> 00:00:12.230
- These are among the
first electric vehicles

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.550
from both companies.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.670
And I think the reason is it's,

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.770
you know this is the most
important part of their business,

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.030
pickup trucks.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.410
- [Narrator] In the race
to electrify their pickups,

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:25.040
the automakers pursued
two distinct strategies.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.352
Ford decided to retrofit
its existing F-150 by adding

00:00:28.352 --> 00:00:32.410
a battery in the place of
its fossil fuel engine.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.730
GM chose a more challenging path

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.890
by designing a new battery system

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.060
and vehicles from the ground up.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.970
So, how did each company race

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:43.757
to develop its new electric vehicles and

00:00:43.757 --> 00:00:46.248
what sets Ford and GM technology apart in

00:00:46.248 --> 00:00:49.722
the highly competitive EV truck race?

00:00:49.722 --> 00:00:51.354
Earlier this year,

00:00:51.354 --> 00:00:55.190
General Motors revealed its Silverado EV,

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.948
a plug-in version of
GM's top selling vehicle

00:00:57.948 --> 00:01:01.057
that will go on sale
in the spring of 2023.

00:01:01.057 --> 00:01:03.833
(bright music)

00:01:03.833 --> 00:01:07.660
- It will offer a revolutionary
mix of capability,

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:09.570
performance, safety,

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.066
flexibility and design.

00:01:11.066 --> 00:01:13.767
- GM started very early on

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:15.269
with sort of a ground up approach.

00:01:15.269 --> 00:01:16.640
You know they decided,

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.670
okay, we don't want to
just do one or two EVs.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:21.030
We tried that in the past.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.130
We haven't gotten very far.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:23.920
We want to do a bunch of models.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.980
- Our clean slate approach allowed us

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.136
to create a new body architecture

00:01:28.136 --> 00:01:29.399
which efficiently leverages

00:01:29.399 --> 00:01:33.290
the available 24 module
Ultium battery pack.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.670
- [Narrator] All of GM's
new EVs will be built on

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:38.340
the company's Ultium battery platform

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:41.432
which GM developed in-house from scratch.

00:01:41.432 --> 00:01:43.729
The electric Silverado will also use

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:46.292
the Ultium system when it is released

00:01:46.292 --> 00:01:48.750
in spring of 2023,

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.506
with prices ranging from about $40,000

00:01:51.506 --> 00:01:53.765
to $105,000.

00:01:53.765 --> 00:01:57.484
One of the Silverado's biggest
selling points is its range.

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:59.250
Thanks to GM's investment,

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:00.470
the Ultium system,

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.840
a Silverado's expected
to have a 400 mile range

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:04.721
on some models.

00:02:04.721 --> 00:02:06.978
That's more than Rivian's R1T,

00:02:06.978 --> 00:02:09.103
which can travel 314 miles

00:02:09.103 --> 00:02:10.940
and the F-150 Lightning,

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.312
which is expected to have a
range of around 300 miles.

00:02:14.312 --> 00:02:15.690
- I think for years,

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.266
the perception's been
that GM has been ahead

00:02:18.266 --> 00:02:20.020
on their electric vehicle strategy.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:20.853
I mean,

00:02:20.853 --> 00:02:23.509
as far back as 2017 GM
started talking about

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:25.004
an all electric future.

00:02:25.004 --> 00:02:26.640
Shortly thereafter,

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:27.930
they started you know,

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.760
giving us targets of how many models,

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:30.593
you know,

00:02:30.593 --> 00:02:32.790
a few dozen models by the early 2020s.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.420
You know I think all of those things were

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.630
in motion at a point

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:38.059
where Wall Street was kind of asking Ford,

00:02:38.059 --> 00:02:38.892
you know,

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.593
where is where all these elements,

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:41.426
you know,

00:02:41.426 --> 00:02:44.141
where is your EV strategy
going essentially?

00:02:44.141 --> 00:02:46.580
- [Narrator] Just a day before GM unveiled

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.030
this new Silverado,

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:48.863
Ford announced

00:02:48.863 --> 00:02:51.534
that it was doubling down
its manufacturing goals

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:52.767
for its EV pickup,

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:55.192
the F-150 Lightning in response to

00:02:55.192 --> 00:02:58.827
an unexpectedly high
number of reservations.

00:02:58.827 --> 00:03:02.964
That news sent Ford stock
surging on January 4th

00:03:02.964 --> 00:03:07.363
and helped propel the automakers
market valuation beyond

00:03:07.363 --> 00:03:11.520
that of GM for the first time since 2016.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.410
- Their stock price went up
I think 11 or 12% that day,

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:18.410
which is until recently kind
of unheard of for an automaker.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:19.243
I mean,

00:03:19.243 --> 00:03:21.370
these things trade like
manufacturing stocks kind of boring.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.470
And so it was,

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.440
it was definitely some
gamesmanship I think,

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:25.273
Ford trying to steal

00:03:25.273 --> 00:03:27.240
a bit of a bit of GM's thunder on its,

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.055
on its Silverado truck.

00:03:29.055 --> 00:03:30.670
- [Narrator] The move comes as

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:34.160
the century old rivalry
between GM and Ford is moving

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:36.192
into the electric vehicle age.

00:03:36.192 --> 00:03:37.690
- [Mike] These companies,

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.980
they've battled in just about every facet

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.480
of the auto industry.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:42.380
And, you know,

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.613
the companies don't really
like each other that much.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.630
- [Narrator] Ford
followed a different path,

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.740
than GM to electrify its pickup.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.660
Rather than create a new
EV from the ground up,

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:56.240
Ford's strategy for
the F-150 Lightning was

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.090
to retrofit an existing
F150 and turn it into

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.032
an EV.

00:04:00.032 --> 00:04:01.566
- [Reporter] Mr. President.

00:04:01.566 --> 00:04:02.417
- This sucker's quick.

00:04:02.417 --> 00:04:05.960
- The decision on Ford's part was, well,

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.400
we want to get into market

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.299
with some of the cars that
we know our customers love.

00:04:10.299 --> 00:04:12.530
We already have strong sort

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.564
of brands with the F-150 pickup truck,

00:04:15.564 --> 00:04:16.850
the Mustang.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:18.330
So let's work with that.

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:20.230
- [Narrator] Unlike the Silverado EV,

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:23.044
which looks very different
from its gas fed predecessor,

00:04:23.044 --> 00:04:24.884
the Silverado 1500,

00:04:24.884 --> 00:04:27.940
the F-150 Lightning is
similar aesthetically

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:30.352
to its fuel powered older sibling.

00:04:30.352 --> 00:04:32.500
- And so in the case of the F150,

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.050
they essentially modified
a gas powered pickup truck,

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:37.120
you know,

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.373
took out the engine transmission,

00:04:39.373 --> 00:04:41.580
put in a big battery pack

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.680
and the electric motors
and everything they needed.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:44.840
- [Narrator] Engineering

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.780
a wholly new electric truck
would have taken longer

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:48.750
to develop.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.221
The retrofit enabled Ford

00:04:50.221 --> 00:04:54.128
to move quickly and beat GM
to market by over a year.

00:04:54.128 --> 00:04:56.544
It also allowed Ford
to leverage its scale,

00:04:56.544 --> 00:04:59.531
since the Lightning uses
many of the same parts

00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:02.710
as as a conventional F-150.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.650
Ford priced the F-150 Lightning

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.520
at around $40,000 for a base model.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.398
High-end models top out
in the high 90 thousands.

00:05:10.398 --> 00:05:11.650
- [Announcer] Popping

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:14.330
the hood has been completely redefined

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.840
at the mega power frunk.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.159
- It's got a huge front
trunk called a frunk,

00:05:18.159 --> 00:05:18.992
you know,

00:05:18.992 --> 00:05:20.650
and so they've made a big deal about,

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.080
hey, you've got lockable storage now

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.450
for the first time in a pickup truck.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.760
- [Narrator] GM's trucks
are sold under two brands,

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.173
Chevy and GMC.

00:05:28.173 --> 00:05:29.420
In some years,

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:31.240
GM's pickup sales under

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:34.713
those two brands have
eclipsed total F series sales.

00:05:34.713 --> 00:05:37.899
But the F-150 has long been
the most popular vehicle

00:05:37.899 --> 00:05:40.930
in the country outselling all other cars,

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:42.836
trucks and SUV's.

00:05:42.836 --> 00:05:45.451
But it remains unclear
if customers will follow

00:05:45.451 --> 00:05:48.062
the brand into its electric future.

00:05:48.062 --> 00:05:50.235
- That's the big question hanging over

00:05:50.235 --> 00:05:52.560
the whole industry right now is all

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.440
these models are coming are there,

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:55.273
you know,

00:05:55.273 --> 00:05:58.090
how much organic interest
is there among consumers?

00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.640
- [Announcer] Those up to the job site.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.700
- [Narrator] Ford has been
aggressively promoting

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:03.510
the F-150 lightening to make

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:06.160
the case that their new
vehicle's features surpass

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:07.767
the gasoline model.

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.008
One ad shows a family
using their Lightening

00:06:10.008 --> 00:06:14.478
to provide backup power to their house.

00:06:14.478 --> 00:06:18.281
Ford said it has 200,000
Lightning reservations.

00:06:18.281 --> 00:06:19.239
For context,

00:06:19.239 --> 00:06:20.810
that's more than a quarter

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:24.693
of the number of F series
vehicles the company sold in 2021,

00:06:24.693 --> 00:06:27.782
But these reservations
are not a firm commitment.

00:06:27.782 --> 00:06:31.099
- These are not binding
200,000 reservations.

00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:33.423
I mean anyone can just walk away from it.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:35.900
But I think Ford is looking at this,

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:38.960
like this could move
faster than we thought.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.230
- [Narrator] Sales for
electric vehicles rose 88% year

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:43.424
over year in 2021.

00:06:43.424 --> 00:06:45.557
- Both these companies realize that

00:06:45.557 --> 00:06:47.550
if we're gonna have success here,

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.080
we're going to have to
carry these products

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:51.370
that have delivered so much value

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:53.530
and so much profit for these companies,

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.740
these big pickup trucks.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.570
You know that rivalry seems like it's

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:58.890
as sharp as ever as both companies try

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.890
to sort of position themselves for that.

00:07:04.825 --> 00:07:07.408
(bright music)

